  "articleBody": "Installing basement trim might seem straightforward, but there are a few common pitfalls that can really mess up the final look. Knowing what to avoid can save you a lot of frustration and wasted material. First off, under-ordering material is a big mistake. Always measure accurately and then add a little extra for cuts and any mishaps. You'd rather have a bit left over than run out mid-project and have to wait for more. Another frequent error is poor measurement at corners and irregular walls. Basements, especially older ones, often aren't perfectly square, so taking your time and using the right tools for precise cuts is essential for a seamless finish. A huge one is failing to confirm your layout before you start cutting. Just like with flooring, it's smart to do a dry run or at least visualize how the pieces will fit together, especially around doorways or other features. If you're integrating trim with new tile, make sure the tile has fully cured before you even think about installing trim; rushing this can lead to issues. When your basement has uneven walls or complex transitions, getting a qualified pro like HH Remodeling LLC involved makes a huge difference in achieving a clean, professional result.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
